\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Conceptual comparison of the existing locally dependent modeling paradigm versus our zero-shot transferable paradigm. Under the existing paradigm, models require target-city OD observations to retrain or calibrate parameters. In our paradigm, we learn transferable origin production structures from source City A, recover decay from target aggregate data, and map attraction from local open features in target City B, enabling zero-shot transfer without target-city OD surveys.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:conceptual_framework}{{2}{4}{Conceptual comparison of the existing locally dependent modeling paradigm versus our zero-shot transferable paradigm. Under the existing paradigm, models require target-city OD observations to retrain or calibrate parameters. In our paradigm, we learn transferable origin production structures from source City A, recover decay from target aggregate data, and map attraction from local open features in target City B, enabling zero-shot transfer without target-city OD surveys}{figure.2}{}}
